## Real-Time Chat and Audio Messaging

### How It Works

After a patient books an appointment and the doctor confirms it, both parties can communicate in real-time through the platform. The chat is linked to the confirmed appointment.

```
Patient books appointment
  -> Doctor confirms
    -> "Chat with Dr. X" button appears on patient's appointment card
    -> "Chat with Patient Y" button appears on doctor's appointment list
    -> Both can send text messages and voice messages
    -> Messages appear instantly via Socket.IO
```

### Architecture

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    BROWSER (Patient or Doctor)                │
│                                                              │
│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌──────────────┐  ┌──────────────────┐   │
│  │ ChatBox UI  │  │AudioRecorder │  │  AudioMessage     │   │
│  │ (text input)│  │(Microphone)  │  │  (playback)       │   │
│  └──────┬──────┘  └──────┬───────┘  └────────┬─────────┘   │
│         │                │                     │              │
│         ▼                ▼                     ▼              │
│  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │              Socket.IO Client                        │    │
│  │  emit("send_message", {...})                         │    │
│  │  on("new_message", callback)                         │    │
│  │  emit("start_recording")                             │    │
│  │  emit("stop_recording")                              │    │
│  └──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────┘    │
└─────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
                    WebSocket connection
                              │
                              ▼
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              FLASK-SOCKETIO SERVER                           │
│                                                              │
│  @socketio.on("send_message")                                │
│    -> Save to ChatMessage table                               │
│    -> emit("new_message") to receiver's room                 │
│                                                              │
│  @socketio.on("start_recording")                             │
│    -> Notify sender that recording started                   │
│                                                              │
│  @socketio.on("stop_recording")                              │
│    -> Receive audio blob                                     │
│    -> Save to uploads/voice_messages/                        │
│    -> Create VoiceMessage record                             │
│    -> emit("new_message") with audio_path to receiver        │
│                                                              │
│  @socketio.on("join_room")                                   │
│    -> Add user to appointment chat room                      │
│                                                              │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Socket.IO Events

| Event | Direction | Payload | Description |
|-------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| join_room | Client -> Server | { appointment_id, user_id } | Join a chat room |
| user_joined | Server -> Client | { user_id, name } | Notify others in room |
| send_message | Client -> Server | { sender_id, receiver_id, appointment_id, message_type, content } | Send text or audio message |
| new_message | Server -> Client | { id, sender_id, sender_name, message_type, content, audio_path, audio_duration, created_at } | Receive new message |
| start_recording | Client -> Server | { user_id, appointment_id } | Audio recording started |
| recording_started | Server -> Client | { user_id } | Notify other user |
| stop_recording | Client -> Server | { user_id, appointment_id, audio_blob } | Stop and send audio |
| voice_uploaded | Server -> Client | { message_id, audio_path, audio_duration } | Audio saved confirmation |
| typing | Client -> Server | { user_id } | User is typing |
| user_typing | Server -> Client | { user_id, name } | Show typing indicator |
| mark_read | Client -> Server | { message_id } | Mark message as read |
| message_read | Server -> Client | { message_id } | Read receipt confirmation |

### Frontend Components

#### ChatBox Component

```jsx
// Shared between patient and doctor dashboards
// Receives: appointmentId, otherUserId, otherUserName

import { useState, useEffect, useRef } from "react";
import { io } from "socket.io-client";
import AudioRecorder from "./AudioRecorder";
import AudioMessage from "./AudioMessage";

function ChatBox({ appointmentId, currentUserId, otherUserId, otherUserName }) {
  const [messages, setMessages] = useState([]);
  const [inputText, setInputText] = useState("");
  const [isTyping, setIsTyping] = useState(false);
  const [isOnline, setIsOnline] = useState(false);
  const socketRef = useRef(null);
  const messagesEndRef = useRef(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    // Connect to Socket.IO server
    socketRef.current = io(SOCKET_URL, {
      auth: { token: localStorage.getItem("token") }
    });

    // Join the appointment chat room
    socketRef.current.emit("join_room", {
      appointment_id: appointmentId,
      user_id: currentUserId
    });

    // Listen for new messages
    socketRef.current.on("new_message", (msg) => {
      setMessages(prev => [...prev, msg]);
    });

    // Listen for typing indicator
    socketRef.current.on("user_typing", () => setIsTyping(true));
    socketRef.current.on("user_stop_typing", () => setIsTyping(false));

    // Listen for online status
    socketRef.current.on("user_online", () => setIsOnline(true));
    socketRef.current.on("user_offline", () => setIsOnline(false));

    // Load existing chat history
    loadHistory();

    return () => socketRef.current?.disconnect();
  }, [appointmentId]);

  const loadHistory = async () => {
    const res = await authFetch(
      `${API_BASE}/api/chat/history/${currentUserId}/${otherUserId}?appointment=${appointmentId}`
    );
    const data = await res.json();
    setMessages(data.messages);
  };

  const sendTextMessage = () => {
    if (!inputText.trim()) return;
    socketRef.current.emit("send_message", {
      sender_id: currentUserId,
      receiver_id: otherUserId,
      appointment_id: appointmentId,
      message_type: "text",
      content: inputText
    });
    setInputText("");
  };

  const sendVoiceMessage = async (audioBlob, duration) => {
    // Upload audio file first
    const formData = new FormData();
    formData.append("audio", audioBlob, "voice.webm");
    formData.append("sender_id", currentUserId);
    formData.append("receiver_id", otherUserId);
    formData.append("appointment_id", appointmentId);
    formData.append("duration", duration);

    const res = await authFetch(`${API_BASE}/api/chat/voice-upload`, {
      method: "POST",
      headers: {},  // Let browser set Content-Type for FormData
      body: formData
    });
    const data = await res.json();

    // Send message via socket with audio path
    socketRef.current.emit("send_message", {
      sender_id: currentUserId,
      receiver_id: otherUserId,
      appointment_id: appointmentId,
      message_type: "audio",
      audio_path: data.audio_path,
      audio_duration: duration
    });
  };

  return (
    <div className="chat-box">
      <div className="chat-header">
        <span className="chat-name">{otherUserName}</span>
        <span className={`online-status ${isOnline ? "online" : "offline"}`}>
          {isOnline ? "Online" : "Offline"}
        </span>
      </div>

      <div className="chat-messages">
        {messages.map((msg) => (
          <div key={msg.id} className={`chat-bubble ${msg.sender_id === currentUserId ? "sent" : "received"}`}>
            {msg.message_type === "text" ? (
              <span className="text-message">{msg.content}</span>
            ) : (
              <AudioMessage
                audioSrc={`${API_BASE}/api/chat/voice/${msg.audio_path}`}
                duration={msg.audio_duration}
                isSent={msg.sender_id === currentUserId}
              />
            )}
            <span className="message-time">
              {new Date(msg.created_at).toLocaleTimeString([], { hour: "2-digit", minute: "2-digit" })}
            </span>
          </div>
        ))}
        {isTyping && <div className="typing-indicator">{otherUserName} is typing...</div>}
        <div ref={messagesEndRef} />
      </div>

      <div className="chat-input">
        <input
          value={inputText}
          onChange={(e) => {
            setInputText(e.target.value);
            socketRef.current.emit("typing", { user_id: currentUserId });
          }}
          onKeyPress={(e) => e.key === "Enter" && sendTextMessage()}
          placeholder="Type a message..."
        />
        <AudioRecorder onRecordingComplete={sendVoiceMessage} />
        <button onClick={sendTextMessage}>Send</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

#### AudioRecorder Component

```jsx
// Records audio from microphone using MediaRecorder API
// Returns audio blob and duration when recording stops

import { useState, useRef } from "react";

function AudioRecorder({ onRecordingComplete }) {
  const [isRecording, setIsRecording] = useState(false);
  const [recordingTime, setRecordingTime] = useState(0);
  const mediaRecorderRef = useRef(null);
  const audioChunksRef = useRef([]);
  const timerRef = useRef(null);

  const startRecording = async () => {
    const stream = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({ audio: true });
    const mediaRecorder = new MediaRecorder(stream, {
      mimeType: "audio/webm;codecs=opus"
    });

    mediaRecorderRef.current = mediaRecorder;
    audioChunksRef.current = [];

    mediaRecorder.ondataavailable = (event) => {
      audioChunksRef.current.push(event.data);
    };

    mediaRecorder.onstop = () => {
      const audioBlob = new Blob(audioChunksRef.current, { type: "audio/webm" });
      const duration = recordingTime;
      onRecordingComplete(audioBlob, duration);
      stream.getTracks().forEach(track => track.stop());
      setRecordingTime(0);
    };

    mediaRecorder.start();
    setIsRecording(true);

    // Start timer
    timerRef.current = setInterval(() => {
      setRecordingTime(prev => prev + 1);
    }, 1000);
  };

  const stopRecording = () => {
    mediaRecorderRef.current?.stop();
    setIsRecording(false);
    clearInterval(timerRef.current);
  };

  const formatTime = (seconds) => {
    const m = Math.floor(seconds / 60);
    const s = seconds % 60;
    return `${m}:${s.toString().padStart(2, "0")}`;
  };

  return (
    <div className="audio-recorder">
      {isRecording ? (
        <div className="recording-active">
          <span className="recording-dot" />
          <span className="recording-time">{formatTime(recordingTime)}</span>
          <button onClick={stopRecording} className="stop-btn">Stop</button>
        </div>
      ) : (
        <button onClick={startRecording} className="mic-btn" title="Record voice message">
          Mic
        </button>
      )}
    </div>
  );
}
```

#### AudioMessage Component

```jsx
// Plays back audio messages with play/pause controls

import { useState, useRef } from "react";

function AudioMessage({ audioSrc, duration, isSent }) {
  const [isPlaying, setIsPlaying] = useState(false);
  const [progress, setProgress] = useState(0);
  const audioRef = useRef(null);

  const togglePlay = () => {
    if (isPlaying) {
      audioRef.current.pause();
    } else {
      audioRef.current.play();
    }
    setIsPlaying(!isPlaying);
  };

  const formatDuration = (sec) => {
    const m = Math.floor(sec / 60);
    const s = Math.floor(sec % 60);
    return `${m}:${s.toString().padStart(2, "0")}`;
  };

  return (
    <div className={`audio-message ${isSent ? "sent" : "received"}`}>
      <audio
        ref={audioRef}
        src={audioSrc}
        onTimeUpdate={() => {
          const pct = (audioRef.current.currentTime / audioRef.current.duration) * 100;
          setProgress(pct);
        }}
        onEnded={() => setIsPlaying(false)}
      />
      <button onClick={togglePlay} className="play-btn">
        {isPlaying ? "Pause" : "Play"}
      </button>
      <div className="audio-progress-bar">
        <div className="audio-progress-fill" style={{ width: `${progress}%` }} />
      </div>
      <span className="audio-duration">{formatDuration(duration)}</span>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Backend Socket Handler

```python
# backend/socket_handler.py

from flask_socketio import SocketIO, emit, join_room, leave_room
from models import db, ChatMessage, VoiceMessage
import os
import base64

socketio = SocketIO(cors_allowed_origins="*", max_http_buffer_size=10 * 1024 * 1024)

def init_socketio(app):
    socketio.init_app(app)

# Track online users
online_users = {}

@socketio.on("connect")
def handle_connect():
    user_id = None  # Extract from auth token
    print(f"Client connected: {user_id}")

@socketio.on("disconnect")
def handle_disconnect():
    user_id = None  # Extract from auth token
    if user_id in online_users:
        del online_users[user_id]

@socketio.on("join_room")
def handle_join_room(data):
    appointment_id = data["appointment_id"]
    user_id = data["user_id"]
    room = f"appointment_{appointment_id}"
    join_room(room)
    online_users[user_id] = {"room": room, "sid": None}
    emit("user_joined", {"user_id": user_id}, room=room, include_self=False)

@socketio.on("leave_room")
def handle_leave_room(data):
    room = f"appointment_{data['appointment_id']}"
    leave_room(room)

@socketio.on("send_message")
def handle_send_message(data):
    sender_id = data["sender_id"]
    receiver_id = data["receiver_id"]
    appointment_id = data["appointment_id"]
    message_type = data.get("message_type", "text")
    content = data.get("content", "")
    audio_path = data.get("audio_path", None)
    audio_duration = data.get("audio_duration", None)

    # Save message to database
    msg = ChatMessage(
        sender_id=sender_id,
        receiver_id=receiver_id,
        appointment_id=appointment_id,
        message_type=message_type,
        content=content,
        audio_path=audio_path,
        audio_duration=audio_duration,
        is_read=False
    )
    db.session.add(msg)
    db.session.commit()

    # Emit to the chat room
    room = f"appointment_{appointment_id}"
    emit("new_message", {
        "id": msg.id,
        "sender_id": sender_id,
        "receiver_id": receiver_id,
        "message_type": message_type,
        "content": content,
        "audio_path": audio_path,
        "audio_duration": audio_duration,
        "created_at": msg.created_at.isoformat()
    }, room=room, include_self=False)

@socketio.on("typing")
def handle_typing(data):
    room = data.get("room")
    emit("user_typing", {"user_id": data["user_id"]}, room=room, include_self=False)

@socketio.on("stop_typing")
def handle_stop_typing(data):
    room = data.get("room")
    emit("user_stop_typing", {"user_id": data["user_id"]}, room=room, include_self=False)

@socketio.on("mark_read")
def handle_mark_read(data):
    message_id = data["message_id"]
    msg = ChatMessage.query.get(message_id)
    if msg:
        msg.is_read = True
        db.session.commit()
        emit("message_read", {"message_id": message_id}, room=data.get("room"))
```

### Voice Message Upload Endpoint

```python
# In backend/app.py

import os
from werkzeug.utils import secure_filename

VOICE_FOLDER = "uploads/voice_messages"
os.makedirs(VOICE_FOLDER, exist_ok=True)

@app.route("/api/chat/voice-upload", methods=["POST"])
def upload_voice_message():
    if "audio" not in request.files:
        return jsonify({"message": "No audio file"}), 400

    audio = request.files["audio"]
    sender_id = request.form.get("sender_id")
    receiver_id = request.form.get("receiver_id")
    appointment_id = request.form.get("appointment_id")
    duration = request.form.get("duration", 0)

    filename = f"voice_{sender_id}_{datetime.now().strftime('%Y%m%d%H%M%S')}.webm"
    filepath = os.path.join(VOICE_FOLDER, filename)
    audio.save(filepath)

    file_size = os.path.getsize(filepath)

    return jsonify({
        "audio_path": filename,
        "audio_duration": float(duration),
        "file_size": file_size
    }), 201


@app.route("/api/chat/voice/<filename>")
def serve_voice_message(filename):
    return send_from_directory(VOICE_FOLDER, filename)
```

### Chat History Endpoint

```python
@app.route("/api/chat/history/<int:user1_id>/<int:user2_id>")
def get_chat_history(user1_id, user2_id):
    appointment_id = request.args.get("appointment")

    query = ChatMessage.query.filter(
        ((ChatMessage.sender_id == user1_id) & (ChatMessage.receiver_id == user2_id)) |
        ((ChatMessage.sender_id == user2_id) & (ChatMessage.receiver_id == user1_id))
    )

    if appointment_id:
        query = query.filter_by(appointment_id=int(appointment_id))

    messages = query.order_by(ChatMessage.created_at.asc()).all()

    return jsonify({
        "messages": [
            {
                "id": m.id,
                "sender_id": m.sender_id,
                "receiver_id": m.receiver_id,
                "message_type": m.message_type,
                "content": m.content,
                "audio_path": m.audio_path,
                "audio_duration": m.audio_duration,
                "is_read": m.is_read,
                "created_at": m.created_at.isoformat()
            }
            for m in messages
        ]
    })


@app.route("/api/chat/unread/<int:user_id>")
def get_unread_count(user_id):
    count = ChatMessage.query.filter_by(
        receiver_id=user_id, is_read=False
    ).count()
    return jsonify({"unread_count": count})
```

