## Implementation Phases

### Phase 0: Fix Existing Bugs (Days 1-3)

- Remove conflicting backend/server.js
- Fix medicine and appointment data shape mismatches (wrap in {medicines: [...]} and {appointments: [...]})
- Add missing endpoints (medicine status, appointment status, notification read/delete)
- Fix hardcoded vitals on dashboard home (fetch from API)
- Fix patient logout to clear all localStorage keys
- Fetch doctor list from API instead of hardcoded values

### Phase 1: Authentication and Security (Days 4-6)

- Add bcrypt password hashing to User model
- Add JWT token authentication with flask-jwt-extended
- Create authFetch helper in src/api.js with token injection
- Add protected route wrappers on frontend
- Add role-based route guards (patient cannot access /doctor, etc.)

### Phase 2: Core Data Flow (Days 7-14)

- Build doctor search page with name and specialization filters
- Add search query parameters to /api/doctors endpoint
- Build appointment booking form (patient selects doctor, date, time, reason)
- Add doctor_id field to Appointment model and migration
- Build doctor appointment management (confirm/decline)
- Add dosage, frequency, timing fields to Medicine model
- Create database migration for new Medicine columns
- Build medicine schedule endpoint and patient medicine tracking UI
- Seed additional doctor and patient data

### Phase 3: Recovery Plan End-to-End (Days 15-20)

- Build /api/doctor/:id/summary endpoint (patient list with recovery scores)
- Build /api/doctor/:id/patients/:id/overview endpoint (single patient detail)
- Verify recovery plan creation and daily task generation flow
- Build doctor dashboard with real data from API
- Build patient detail view for doctor
- Verify patient can view recovery plan and mark tasks done
- Verify recovery progress updates correctly

### Phase 4: Real-Time Chat and Audio Messaging (Days 21-28)

- Install Flask-SocketIO on backend
- Install socket.io-client on frontend
- Add ChatMessage and VoiceMessage models to database
- Create backend/socket_handler.py with Socket.IO event handlers
- Build voice message upload endpoint (save audio files to uploads/voice_messages/)
- Build voice message streaming endpoint
- Build chat history endpoint
- Build unread message count endpoint
- Create ChatBox.jsx shared component (text input, message list, typing indicator)
- Create AudioRecorder.jsx component (MediaRecorder API, recording timer, stop button)
- Create AudioMessage.jsx component (audio playback, play/pause, progress bar, duration)
- Add "Chat with Doctor" button to patient appointment card (visible after confirmation)
